return [
    // xxe
    'XML external entity (XXE) injection' => 'Injeksi XML external entity (XXE)',
    "In this section, we'll explain what XML external entity injection is, describe some common examples, explain how to find and exploit various kinds of XXE injection, and summarize how to prevent XXE injection attacks." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan apa itu injeksi XML external entity, memberi beberapa contoh umum, menunjukkan cara menemukan dan mengeksploitasi berbagai jenis XXE, serta merangkum cara mencegahnya.',
    'What is XML external entity injection?' => 'Apa itu injeksi XML external entity?',
    "XML external entity injection (also known as XXE) is a web security vulnerability that allows an attacker to interfere with an application's processing of XML data. It often allows an attacker to view files on the application server filesystem, and to interact with any back-end or external systems that the application itself can access." => 'Injeksi XML external entity (dikenal sebagai XXE) adalah kerentanan keamanan web yang memungkinkan penyerang memengaruhi cara aplikasi memproses data XML. Celah ini sering membuat penyerang dapat membaca file di sistem berkas server aplikasi serta berinteraksi dengan sistem back-end atau eksternal yang dapat diakses aplikasi.',
    'In some situations, an attacker can escalate an XXE attack to compromise the underlying server or other back-end infrastructure, by leveraging the XXE vulnerability to perform server-side request forgery (SSRF) attacks.' => 'Dalam sejumlah skenario, penyerang dapat memperluas serangan XXE untuk menguasai server atau infrastruktur back-end dengan memanfaatkannya melakukan serangan server-side request forgery (SSRF).',
    "If you're already familiar with the basic concepts behind XXE vulnerabilities and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below." => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar kerentanan XXE dan ingin langsung berlatih eksploitasi pada target realistis yang sengaja dibuat rentan, akses semua lab topik ini lewat tautan di bawah.',
    'View all XXE labs' => 'Lihat semua lab XXE',
    'How do XXE vulnerabilities arise?' => 'Bagaimana kerentanan XXE muncul?',
    'Some applications use the XML format to transmit data between the browser and the server. Applications that do this virtually always use a standard library or platform API to process the XML data on the server. XXE vulnerabilities arise because the XML specification contains various potentially dangerous features, and standard parsers support these features even if they are not normally used by the application.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi memakai format XML untuk bertukar data antara browser dan server dengan pustaka standar atau API platform. Kerentanan XXE muncul karena spesifikasi XML memiliki fitur yang berisiko tinggi dan parser standar mendukung fitur tersebut secara bawaan meskipun aplikasi sebenarnya tidak membutuhkannya.',
    'Learn about the XML format, DTDs, and external entities' => 'Pelajari format XML, DTD, dan external entity',
    'XML external entities are a type of custom XML entity whose defined values are loaded from outside of the DTD in which they are declared. External entities are particularly interesting from a security perspective because they allow an entity to be defined based on the contents of a file path or URL.' => 'XML external entity adalah jenis entitas XML kustom yang nilainya dimuat dari luar DTD tempat deklarasinya berada. Dari sisi keamanan, fitur ini sangat penting karena memungkinkan sebuah entitas didefinisikan berdasarkan isi path file atau URL.',
    'What are the types of XXE attacks?' => 'Apa saja jenis serangan XXE?',
    'There are various types of XXE attacks:' => 'Terdapat beberapa jenis serangan XXE:',
    '[[A0]]Exploiting XXE to retrieve files[[/A0]], where an external entity is defined containing the contents of a file, and returned in the application\'s response.' => '[[A0]]Mengeksploitasi XXE untuk mengambil file[[/A0]], saat external entity berisi isi file dikembalikan di dalam respons aplikasi.',
    '[[A0]]Exploiting XXE to perform SSRF attacks[[/A0]], where an external entity is defined based on a URL to a back-end system.' => '[[A0]]Mengeksploitasi XXE untuk melakukan serangan SSRF[[/A0]], saat external entity didefinisikan memakai URL ke sistem back-end.',
    '[[A0]]Exploiting blind XXE exfiltrate data out-of-band[[/A0]], where sensitive data is transmitted from the application server to a system that the attacker controls.' => '[[A0]]Mengeksploitasi blind XXE untuk eksfiltrasi data out-of-band[[/A0]], saat data sensitif dikirim server aplikasi ke sistem milik penyerang.',
    '[[A0]]Exploiting blind XXE to retrieve data via error messages[[/A0]], where the attacker can trigger a parsing error message containing sensitive data.' => '[[A0]]Mengeksploitasi blind XXE untuk mengambil data lewat pesan error[[/A0]], saat penyerang memicu galat parsing yang menampilkan data sensitif.',
    'Exploiting XXE to retrieve files' => 'Mengeksploitasi XXE untuk mengambil file',
    "To perform an XXE injection attack that retrieves an arbitrary file from the server's filesystem, you need to modify the submitted XML in two ways:" => 'Untuk melakukan serangan XXE yang mengambil file sembarang dari server, ubah XML yang dikirim dengan dua langkah:',
    'Introduce (or edit) a [[C0]] element that defines an external entity containing the path to the file.' => 'Tambahkan atau ubah elemen [[C0]] yang mendefinisikan external entity berisi path file target.',
    "Edit a data value in the XML that is returned in the application's response, to make use of the defined external entity." => 'Ubah nilai data dalam XML yang dipantulkan di respons aplikasi agar merujuk pada external entity tersebut.',
    'For example, suppose a shopping application checks for the stock level of a product by submitting the following XML to the server:' => 'Misalnya, sebuah aplikasi toko online mengecek stok produk dengan mengirim XML berikut ke server:',
    'The application performs no particular defenses against XXE attacks, so you can exploit the XXE vulnerability to retrieve the [[C0]] file by submitting the following XXE payload:' => 'Aplikasi ini tidak menerapkan perlindungan terhadap XXE, sehingga Anda dapat mengeksploitasinya untuk membaca file [[C0]] menggunakan payload berikut:',
    "This XXE payload defines an external entity [[C0]] whose value is the contents of the [[C1]] file and uses the entity within the [[C2]] value. This causes the application's response to include the contents of the file:" => 'Payload XXE ini mendefinisikan external entity [[C0]] bernilai isi file [[C1]] lalu memakainya pada elemen [[C2]]. Akibatnya, respons aplikasi menampilkan isi file tersebut:',
    "With real-world XXE vulnerabilities, there will often be a large number of data values within the submitted XML, any one of which might be used within the application's response. To test systematically for XXE vulnerabilities, you will generally need to test each data node in the XML individually, by making use of your defined entity and seeing whether it appears within the response." => 'Pada kasus nyata, dokumen XML sering memuat banyak node data yang salah satunya mungkin dipantulkan di respons. Untuk menguji XXE secara sistematis, uji tiap node data satu per satu dengan merujuk entitas yang Anda definisikan dan periksa kemunculannya pada respons.',
    'Exploiting XXE to perform SSRF attacks' => 'Mengeksploitasi XXE untuk melakukan serangan SSRF',
    'Aside from retrieval of sensitive data, the other main impact of XXE attacks is that they can be used to perform server-side request forgery (SSRF). This is a potentially serious vulnerability in which the server-side application can be induced to make HTTP requests to any URL that the server can access.' => 'Selain mengambil data sensitif, dampak utama lain dari XXE adalah kemampuan melancarkan server-side request forgery (SSRF). Ini merupakan celah serius yang membuat aplikasi sisi server mengirim permintaan HTTP ke URL mana pun yang dapat diakses server.',
    "To exploit an XXE vulnerability to perform an SSRF attack, you need to define an external XML entity using the URL that you want to target, and use the defined entity within a data value. If you can use the defined entity within a data value that is returned in the application's response, then you will be able to view the response from the URL within the application's response, and so gain two-way interaction with the back-end system. If not, then you will only be able to perform blind SSRF attacks (which can still have critical consequences)." => 'Untuk melakukan SSRF lewat XXE, definisikan external entity XML berisi URL target lalu pakai di dalam nilai data. Jika nilai tersebut dikembalikan di respons aplikasi, Anda bisa melihat respons sistem back-end secara dua arah. Jika tidak, serangan menjadi blind SSRF yang tetap berisiko tinggi.',
    "In the following XXE example, the external entity will cause the server to make a back-end HTTP request to an internal system within the organization's infrastructure:" => 'Pada contoh XXE berikut, external entity memaksa server mengirim permintaan HTTP back-end ke sistem internal organisasi:',
    'Blind XXE vulnerabilities' => 'Kerentanan blind XXE',
    'Many instances of XXE vulnerabilities are blind. This means that the application does not return the values of any defined external entities in its responses, and so direct retrieval of server-side files is not possible.' => 'Banyak celah XXE bersifat blind. Artinya, aplikasi tidak mengembalikan nilai external entity di respons sehingga pembacaan file secara langsung tidak dimungkinkan.',
    'Blind XXE vulnerabilities can still be detected and exploited, but more advanced techniques are required. You can sometimes use out-of-band techniques to find vulnerabilities and exploit them to exfiltrate data. And you can sometimes trigger XML parsing errors that lead to disclosure of sensitive data within error messages.' => 'Kerentanan blind XXE tetap bisa ditemukan dan dieksploitasi dengan teknik lanjutan, seperti interaksi out-of-band untuk mendeteksi dan mengeksfiltrasi data, atau memicu error parsing XML yang membocorkan data sensitif.',
    'Finding and exploiting blind XXE vulnerabilities' => 'Menemukan dan mengeksploitasi kerentanan blind XXE',
    'Finding hidden attack surface for XXE injection' => 'Menemukan permukaan serangan tersembunyi untuk injeksi XXE',
    "Attack surface for XXE injection vulnerabilities is obvious in many cases, because the application's normal HTTP traffic includes requests that contain data in XML format. In other cases, the attack surface is less visible. However, if you look in the right places, you will find XXE attack surface in requests that do not contain any XML." => 'Permukaan serangan XXE kerap terlihat jelas saat lalu lintas HTTP normal memakai format XML. Namun di beberapa aplikasi, celah ini tersembunyi di balik permintaan yang sekilas tidak mengandung XML sama sekali.',
    'XInclude attacks' => 'Serangan XInclude',
    'Some applications receive client-submitted data, embed it on the server-side into an XML document, and then parse the document. An example of this occurs when client-submitted data is placed into a back-end SOAP request, which is then processed by the backend SOAP service.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi menerima input klien, menyisipkannya ke dokumen XML di sisi server, lalu mem-parse dokumen itu, misalnya ketika input pengguna dimasukkan ke permintaan SOAP back-end.',
    "In this situation, you cannot carry out a classic XXE attack, because you don't control the entire XML document and so cannot define or modify a [[C0]] element. However, you might be able to use [[C1]] instead. [[C2]] is a part of the XML specification that allows an XML document to be built from sub-documents. You can place an [[C3]] attack within any data value in an XML document, so the attack can be performed in situations where you only control a single item of data that is placed into a server-side XML document." => 'Pada kondisi ini, XXE klasik tidak dapat dipakai karena Anda tidak mengendalikan seluruh dokumen XML dan tidak bisa mengubah elemen [[C0]]. Sebagai gantinya, gunakan [[C1]], yakni bagian spesifikasi XML untuk menyusun dokumen dari sub-dokumen. Serangan [[C2]] dapat ditempatkan di dalam nilai data mana saja saat Anda hanya menguasai satu item input pada dokumen XML server.',
    'To perform an [[C0]] attack, you need to reference the [[C1]] namespace and provide the path to the file that you wish to include. For example:' => 'Untuk melancarkan serangan [[C0]], rujuk namespace [[C1]] dan tentukan path file yang ingin disertakan. Contohnya:',
    'XXE attacks via file upload' => 'Serangan XXE melalui unggah file',
    'Some applications allow users to upload files which are then processed server-side. Some common file formats use XML or contain XML subcomponents. Examples of XML-based formats are office document formats like DOCX and image formats like SVG.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi mengizinkan pengguna mengunggah file yang diproses di sisi server. Beberapa format umum berbasis XML atau memuat subkomponen XML, seperti dokumen DOCX dan gambar SVG.',
    'For example, an application might allow users to upload images, and process or validate these on the server after they are uploaded. Even if the application expects to receive a format like PNG or JPEG, the image processing library that is being used might support SVG images. Since the SVG format uses XML, an attacker can submit a malicious SVG image and so reach hidden attack surface for XXE vulnerabilities.' => 'Misalnya aplikasi menerima unggahan gambar PNG atau JPEG, tetapi pustaka pemroses gambar di server juga mendukung SVG. Karena SVG menggunakan format XML, penyerang dapat mengunggah SVG berbahaya untuk menjangkau permukaan serangan XXE.',
    'XXE attacks via modified content type' => 'Serangan XXE melalui modifikasi Content-Type',
    'Most POST requests use a default content type that is generated by HTML forms, such as [[C0]]. Some web sites expect to receive requests in this format but will tolerate other content types, including XML.' => 'Sebagian besar permintaan POST memakai tipe konten bawaan form HTML seperti [[C0]]. Beberapa situs mengharapkan format tersebut, namun tetap menerima tipe konten lain termasuk XML.',
    'For example, if a normal request contains the following:' => 'Misalnya, jika permintaan normal terlihat seperti ini:',
    'Then you might be able submit the following request, with the same result:' => 'Anda mungkin dapat mengirim permintaan berikut dengan hasil serupa:',
    'If the application tolerates requests containing XML in the message body, and parses the body content as XML, then you can reach the hidden XXE attack surface simply by reformatting requests to use the XML format.' => 'Jika aplikasi menerima body permintaan berformat XML dan mem-parse isinya sebagai XML, Anda cukup mengubah format permintaan ke XML untuk membuka permukaan serangan XXE.',
    'How to find and test for XXE vulnerabilities' => 'Cara menemukan dan menguji kerentanan XXE',
    "The vast majority of XXE vulnerabilities can be found quickly and reliably using Burp Suite's web vulnerability scanner." => 'Sebagian besar kerentanan XXE dapat ditemukan dengan cepat dan andal menggunakan pemindai kerentanan web.',
    'Manually testing for XXE vulnerabilities generally involves:' => 'Pengujian manual untuk kerentanan XXE umumnya mencakup:',
    'Testing for [[A0]]file retrieval[[/A0]] by defining an external entity based on a well-known operating system file and using that entity in data that is returned in the application\'s response.' => 'Menguji [[A0]]pembacaan file[[/A0]] dengan mendefinisikan external entity ke file sistem operasi umum dan memakainya pada data yang kembali di respons.',
    'Testing for [[A0]]blind XXE vulnerabilities[[/A0]] by defining an external entity based on a URL to a system that you control, and monitoring for interactions with that system. [[A1]]Burp Collaborator[[/A1]] is perfect for this purpose.' => 'Menguji [[A0]]kerentanan blind XXE[[/A0]] dengan mendefinisikan external entity ke URL sistem yang Anda kendalikan lalu memantau interaksinya menggunakan [[A1]]server kolaborator OAST[[/A1]].',
    'Testing for vulnerable inclusion of user-supplied non-XML data within a server-side XML document by using an [[A0]]XInclude attack[[/A0]] to try to retrieve a well-known operating system file.' => 'Menguji penyisipan data non-XML milik pengguna ke dokumen XML sisi server lewat [[A0]]serangan XInclude[[/A0]] untuk mengambil file sistem operasi umum.',
    'Keep in mind that XML is just a data transfer format. Make sure you also test any XML-based functionality for other vulnerabilities like XSS and SQL injection. You may need to encode your payload using XML escape sequences to avoid breaking the syntax, but you may also be able to use this to [[A0]]obfuscate your attack[[/A0]] in order to bypass weak defences.' => 'Ingat bahwa XML hanyalah format transfer data. Uji juga fitur berbasis XML untuk celah lain seperti XSS dan SQL injection. Anda mungkin perlu meng-encode payload memakai escape sequence XML agar sintaks tetap valid, yang sekaligus berguna untuk [[A0]]menyamarkan serangan[[/A0]] guna melewati filter lemah.',
    'How to prevent XXE vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan XXE',
    "Virtually all XXE vulnerabilities arise because the application's XML parsing library supports potentially dangerous XML features that the application does not need or intend to use. The easiest and most effective way to prevent XXE attacks is to disable those features." => 'Hampir semua celah XXE timbul karena pustaka parser XML mendukung fitur berbahaya yang tidak dipakai aplikasi. Cara termudah dan paling efektif adalah menonaktifkan fitur tersebut.',
    'Generally, it is sufficient to disable resolution of external entities and disable support for [[C0]]. This can usually be done via configuration options or by programmatically overriding default behavior. Consult the documentation for your XML parsing library or API for details about how to disable unnecessary capabilities.' => 'Umumnya cukup dengan menonaktifkan resolusi external entity dan dukungan terhadap [[C0]] melalui opsi konfigurasi atau pengaturan programatik pada parser XML yang dipakai.',
    'Find XXE vulnerabilities using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner' => 'Menemukan kerentanan XXE dengan pemindai otomatis',

    // xxe/blind
    "In this section, we'll explain what blind XXE injection is and describe various techniques for finding and exploiting blind XXE vulnerabilities." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan apa itu injeksi blind XXE beserta berbagai teknik untuk menemukan dan mengeksploitasinya.',
    'What is blind XXE?' => 'Apa itu blind XXE?',
    'Blind XXE vulnerabilities arise where the application is vulnerable to XXE injection but does not return the values of any defined external entities within its responses. This means that direct retrieval of server-side files is not possible, and so blind XXE is generally harder to exploit than regular XXE vulnerabilities.' => 'Kerentanan blind XXE muncul ketika aplikasi rentan terhadap injeksi XXE tetapi tidak mengembalikan nilai external entity di dalam responsnya. Pembacaan file secara langsung tidak bisa dilakukan sehingga celah ini lebih sulit dieksploitasi dibanding XXE biasa.',
    'There are two broad ways in which you can find and exploit blind XXE vulnerabilities:' => 'Ada dua pendekatan utama untuk menemukan dan mengeksploitasi blind XXE:',
    'You can trigger out-of-band network interactions, sometimes exfiltrating sensitive data within the interaction data.' => 'Memicu interaksi jaringan out-of-band, terkadang disertai eksfiltrasi data sensitif di dalamnya.',
    'You can trigger XML parsing errors in such a way that the error messages contain sensitive data.' => 'Memicu galat parsing XML sedemikian rupa sehingga pesan galatnya memuat data sensitif.',
    'Detecting blind XXE using out-of-band (OAST) techniques' => 'Mendeteksi blind XXE dengan teknik out-of-band (OAST)',
    'You can often detect blind XXE using the same technique as for [[A0]]XXE SSRF attacks[[/A0]] but triggering the out-of-band network interaction to a system that you control. For example, you would define an external entity as follows:' => 'Anda sering dapat mendeteksi blind XXE memakai teknik mirip [[A0]]serangan XXE SSRF[[/A0]], yaitu memicu interaksi out-of-band ke sistem kendali Anda. Contoh definisi external entity:',
    'You would then make use of the defined entity in a data value within the XML.' => 'Selanjutnya, gunakan entitas tersebut pada salah satu nilai data di dalam XML.',
    'This XXE attack causes the server to make a back-end HTTP request to the specified URL. The attacker can monitor for the resulting DNS lookup and HTTP request, and thereby detect that the XXE attack was successful.' => 'Serangan ini memaksa server mengirim permintaan HTTP back-end ke URL tersebut. Penyerang cukup memantau kueri DNS dan permintaan HTTP yang masuk untuk membuktikan kerentanan.',
    'Sometimes, XXE attacks using regular entities are blocked, due to some input validation by the application or some hardening of the XML parser that is being used. In this situation, you might be able to use XML parameter entities instead. XML parameter entities are a special kind of XML entity which can only be referenced elsewhere within the DTD. For present purposes, you only need to know two things. First, the declaration of an XML parameter entity includes the percent character before the entity name:' => 'Terkadang serangan XXE dengan entitas biasa diblokir oleh validasi input atau pengerasan parser XML. Dalam situasi ini, Anda bisa memakai XML parameter entity yang hanya dapat direferensikan di dalam DTD. Pertama, deklarasinya menyertakan karakter persen sebelum nama entitas:',
    'And second, parameter entities are referenced using the percent character instead of the usual ampersand:' => 'Kedua, parameter entity dipanggil menggunakan karakter persen, bukan ampersand:',
    'This means that you can test for blind XXE using out-of-band detection via XML parameter entities as follows:' => 'Artinya, Anda dapat menguji blind XXE memakai deteksi out-of-band lewat XML parameter entity sebagai berikut:',
    "This XXE payload declares an XML parameter entity called [[C0]] and then uses the entity within the DTD. This will cause a DNS lookup and HTTP request to the attacker's domain, verifying that the attack was successful." => 'Payload ini mendeklarasikan XML parameter entity bernama [[C0]] lalu memakainya di dalam DTD, sehingga memicu DNS lookup dan permintaan HTTP ke domain penyerang.',
    'Exploiting blind XXE to exfiltrate data out-of-band' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind XXE untuk eksfiltrasi data out-of-band',
    "Detecting a blind XXE vulnerability via out-of-band techniques is all very well, but it doesn't actually demonstrate how the vulnerability could be exploited. What an attacker really wants to achieve is to exfiltrate sensitive data. This can be achieved via a blind XXE vulnerability, but it involves the attacker hosting a malicious DTD on a system that they control, and then invoking the external DTD from within the in-band XXE payload." => 'Deteksi blind XXE lewat out-of-band membuktikan adanya celah, namun tujuan utamanya adalah mengekstrak data sensitif. Hal ini dapat dilakukan dengan meng-host DTD berbahaya di server kendali penyerang lalu memanggilnya dari payload XXE.',
    'An example of a malicious DTD to exfiltrate the contents of the [[C0]] file is as follows:' => 'Contoh DTD berbahaya untuk mengekstrak isi file [[C0]] adalah sebagai berikut:',
    'This DTD carries out the following steps:' => 'DTD ini menjalankan langkah-langkah berikut:',
    'Defines an XML parameter entity called [[C0]], containing the contents of the [[C1]] file.' => 'Mendefinisikan XML parameter entity bernama [[C0]] berisi isi file [[C1]].',
    "Defines an XML parameter entity called [[C0]], containing a dynamic declaration of another XML parameter entity called [[C1]]. The [[C2]] entity will be evaluated by making an HTTP request to the attacker's web server containing the value of the [[C3]] entity within the URL query string." => 'Mendefinisikan XML parameter entity bernama [[C0]] berisi deklarasi dinamis entitas [[C1]]. Entitas [[C2]] dievaluasi dengan mengirim permintaan HTTP ke server penyerang sembari membawa nilai [[C3]] pada query string.',
    'Uses the [[C0]] entity, which causes the dynamic declaration of the [[C1]] entity to be performed.' => 'Memanggil entitas [[C0]] sehingga deklarasi dinamis entitas [[C1]] dijalankan.',
    'Uses the [[C0]] entity, so that its value is evaluated by requesting the specified URL.' => 'Memanggil entitas [[C0]] sehingga nilainya dievaluasi dengan mengakses URL target.',
    'The attacker must then host the malicious DTD on a system that they control, normally by loading it onto their own webserver. For example, the attacker might serve the malicious DTD at the following URL:' => 'Penyerang kemudian menempatkan DTD tersebut di server web miliknya, misalnya pada URL berikut:',
    'Finally, the attacker must submit the following XXE payload to the vulnerable application:' => 'Terakhir, penyerang mengirim payload XXE berikut ke aplikasi yang rentan:',
    "This XXE payload declares an XML parameter entity called [[C0]] and then uses the entity within the DTD. This will cause the XML parser to fetch the external DTD from the attacker's server and interpret it inline. The steps defined within the malicious DTD are then executed, and the [[C1]] file is transmitted to the attacker's server." => 'Payload ini mendeklarasikan parameter entity [[C0]] lalu memanggilnya di DTD. Parser XML mengambil DTD eksternal dari server penyerang dan menjalankannya sehingga isi [[C1]] terkirim keluar.',
    'This technique might not work with some file contents, including the newline characters contained in the [[C0]] file. This is because some XML parsers fetch the URL in the external entity definition using an API that validates the characters that are allowed to appear within the URL. In this situation, it might be possible to use the FTP protocol instead of HTTP. Sometimes, it will not be possible to exfiltrate data containing newline characters, and so a file such as [[C1]] can be targeted instead.' => 'Teknik ini terkadang gagal pada file yang mengandung karakter baris baru seperti [[C0]], karena API pengambil URL memvalidasi karakter di URL. Anda dapat mencoba protokol FTP atau menargetkan file satu baris seperti [[C1]].',
    'Exploiting blind XXE to retrieve data via error messages' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind XXE untuk mengambil data lewat pesan error',
    'An alternative approach to exploiting blind XXE is to trigger an XML parsing error where the error message contains the sensitive data that you wish to retrieve. This will be effective if the application returns the resulting error message within its response.' => 'Alternatif lainnya adalah memicu error parsing XML agar pesan galatnya memuat data sensitif. Cara ini efektif bila aplikasi menampilkan pesan error pada respons.',
    'You can trigger an XML parsing error message containing the contents of the [[C0]] file using a malicious external DTD as follows:' => 'Anda dapat memicu pesan error berisi isi file [[C0]] memakai DTD eksternal berikut:',
    'Defines an XML parameter entity called [[C0]], containing a dynamic declaration of another XML parameter entity called [[C1]]. The [[C2]] entity will be evaluated by loading a nonexistent file whose name contains the value of the [[C3]] entity.' => 'Mendefinisikan parameter entity [[C0]] berisi deklarasi dinamis entitas [[C1]], yang dievaluasi dengan mencoba memuat file fiktif bernama nilai dari entitas [[C2]].',
    'Uses the [[C0]] entity, so that its value is evaluated by attempting to load the nonexistent file, resulting in an error message containing the name of the nonexistent file, which is the contents of the [[C1]] file.' => 'Memanggil entitas [[C0]] agar parser mencoba memuat file fiktif dan menghasilkan pesan error berisi nama file tersebut, yaitu isi [[C1]].',
    'Invoking the malicious external DTD will result in an error message like the following:' => 'Pemanggilan DTD eksternal berbahaya tersebut menghasilkan pesan error seperti berikut:',
    'Exploiting blind XXE by repurposing a local DTD' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind XXE dengan memanfaatkan DTD lokal',
    "The preceding technique works fine with an external DTD, but it won't normally work with an internal DTD that is fully specified within the [[C0]] element. This is because the technique involves using an XML parameter entity within the definition of another parameter entity. Per the XML specification, this is permitted in external DTDs but not in internal DTDs. (Some parsers might tolerate it, but many do not.)" => 'Teknik di atas berjalan baik pada DTD eksternal, namun biasanya gagal dalam DTD internal di dalam elemen [[C0]] karena spesifikasi XML melarang pemakaian parameter entity di dalam definisi parameter entity lain pada DTD internal.',
    "So what about blind XXE vulnerabilities when out-of-band interactions are blocked? You can't exfiltrate data via an out-of-band connection, and you can't load an external DTD from a remote server." => 'Lalu bagaimana jika interaksi out-of-band diblokir sehingga DTD eksternal jarak jauh tidak bisa dimuat?',
    "In this situation, it might still be possible to trigger error messages containing sensitive data, due to a loophole in the XML language specification. If a document's DTD uses a hybrid of internal and external DTD declarations, then the internal DTD can redefine entities that are declared in the external DTD. When this happens, the restriction on using an XML parameter entity within the definition of another parameter entity is relaxed." => 'Anda tetap berpeluang memicu pesan error berisi data sensitif lewat celah spesifikasi XML: jika DTD memakai gabungan deklarasi internal dan eksternal, DTD internal dapat mendefinisikan ulang entitas milik DTD eksternal dan batasan pemakaian parameter entity bersarang menjadi longgar.',
    'This means that an attacker can employ the [[A0]]error-based XXE[[/A0]] technique from within an internal DTD, provided the XML parameter entity that they use is redefining an entity that is declared within an external DTD. Of course, if out-of-band connections are blocked, then the external DTD cannot be loaded from a remote location. Instead, it needs to be an external DTD file that is local to the application server. Essentially, the attack involves invoking a DTD file that happens to exist on the local filesystem and repurposing it to redefine an existing entity in a way that triggers a parsing error containing sensitive data. This technique was pioneered by Arseniy Sharoglazov, and ranked #7 in our [[A1]]top 10 web hacking techniques of 2018[[/A1]].' => 'Artinya, teknik [[A0]]XXE berbasis pesan error[[/A0]] dapat dijalankan dari DTD internal asalkan entitas yang didefinisikan ulang berasal dari file DTD eksternal di filesystem lokal server. Serangan ini memanggil file DTD lokal yang sudah ada lalu mengubah salah satu entitasnya untuk memicu error berisi data sensitif.',
    'For example, suppose there is a DTD file on the server filesystem at the location [[C0]], and this DTD file defines an entity called [[C1]]. An attacker can trigger an XML parsing error message containing the contents of the [[C2]] file by submitting a hybrid DTD like the following:' => 'Sebagai contoh, misalkan ada file DTD lokal di [[C0]] yang mendefinisikan entitas [[C1]]. Penyerang dapat memicu error parsing berisi isi [[C2]] lewat DTD hibrida berikut:',
    'Defines an XML parameter entity called [[C0]], containing the contents of the external DTD file that exists on the server filesystem.' => 'Mendefinisikan XML parameter entity bernama [[C0]] yang memuat isi file DTD eksternal di sistem berkas server.',
    'Redefines the XML parameter entity called [[C0]], which is already defined in the external DTD file. The entity is redefined as containing the [[A0]]error-based XXE exploit[[/A0]] that was already described, for triggering an error message containing the contents of the [[C1]] file.' => 'Mendefinisikan ulang parameter entity [[C0]] yang ada di DTD eksternal dengan [[A0]]eksploit XXE berbasis pesan error[[/A0]] guna memicu error berisi isi [[C1]].',
    'Uses the [[C0]] entity, so that the external DTD is interpreted, including the redefined value of the [[C1]] entity. This results in the desired error message.' => 'Memanggil entitas [[C0]] agar DTD eksternal beserta definisi ulang [[C1]] dievaluasi sehingga menghasilkan pesan error yang diinginkan.',
    'Locating an existing DTD file to repurpose' => 'Menemukan file DTD lokal untuk dimanfaatkan ulang',
    'Since this XXE attack involves repurposing an existing DTD on the server filesystem, a key requirement is to locate a suitable file. This is actually quite straightforward. Because the application returns any error messages thrown by the XML parser, you can easily enumerate local DTD files just by attempting to load them from within the internal DTD.' => 'Karena serangan ini mengandalkan DTD lokal di server, Anda perlu menemukan lokasi file yang cocok. Hal ini mudah dilakukan dengan mencoba memuat path DTD umum dari DTD internal dan mengamati pesan error yang dikembalikan aplikasi.',
    'For example, Linux systems using the GNOME desktop environment often have a DTD file at [[C0]]. You can test whether this file is present by submitting the following XXE payload, which will cause an error if the file is missing:' => 'Misalnya, sistem Linux dengan komponen GNOME kerap memiliki file DTD di [[C0]]. Keberadaannya dapat diuji lewat payload berikut yang akan memicu error jika file tidak ditemukan:',
    'After you have tested a list of common DTD files to locate a file that is present, you then need to obtain a copy of the file and review it to find an entity that you can redefine. Since many common systems that include DTD files are open source, you can normally quickly obtain a copy of files through internet search.' => 'Setelah menemukan file DTD yang ada di server, cari salinan file paket open-source tersebut untuk mengidentifikasi nama entitas yang bisa didefinisikan ulang.',

    // xxe/xml-entities
    'XML entities' => 'Entitas XML',
    "In this section, we'll explain some key features of XML that are relevant to understanding [[A0]]XXE vulnerabilities[[/A0]]." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan beberapa fitur utama XML yang relevan untuk memahami [[A0]]kerentanan XXE[[/A0]].',
    'What is XML?' => 'Apa itu XML?',
    'XML stands for "extensible markup language". XML is a language designed for storing and transporting data. Like HTML, XML uses a tree-like structure of tags and data. Unlike HTML, XML does not use predefined tags, and so tags can be given names that describe the data. Earlier in the web\'s history, XML was in vogue as a data transport format (the "X" in "AJAX" stands for "XML"). But its popularity has now declined in favor of the JSON format.' => 'XML adalah singkatan dari "extensible markup language", bahasa yang dirancang untuk menyimpan dan mengirim data menggunakan struktur pohon tag. Tidak seperti HTML, tag XML bebas dinamai sesuai data. Dahulu XML populer sebagai format pertukaran data, sebelum kini banyak digantikan oleh JSON.',
    'What are XML entities?' => 'Apa itu entitas XML?',
    'XML entities are a way of representing an item of data within an XML document, instead of using the data itself. Various entities are built in to the specification of the XML language. For example, the entities [[C0]] and [[C1]] represent the characters [[C2]] and [[C3]]. These are metacharacters used to denote XML tags, and so must generally be represented using their entities when they appear within data.' => 'Entitas XML adalah cara merepresentasikan nilai data di dalam dokumen XML tanpa menuliskannya langsung. Sejumlah entitas sudah bawaan dalam spesifikasi XML, misalnya [[C0]] dan [[C1]] untuk karakter [[C2]] dan [[C3]] yang merupakan metakarakter tag XML.',
    'What is document type definition?' => 'Apa itu document type definition (DTD)?',
    'The XML document type definition (DTD) contains declarations that can define the structure of an XML document, the types of data values it can contain, and other items. The DTD is declared within the optional [[C0]] element at the start of the XML document. The DTD can be fully self-contained within the document itself (known as an "internal DTD") or can be loaded from elsewhere (known as an "external DTD") or can be hybrid of the two.' => 'Document Type Definition (DTD) XML berisi deklarasi yang mengatur struktur dokumen XML dan jenis data di dalamnya. DTD dideklarasikan pada elemen opsional [[C0]] di awal dokumen, dan dapat bersifat internal, eksternal, atau gabungan keduanya.',
    'What are XML custom entities?' => 'Apa itu entitas kustom XML?',
    'XML allows custom entities to be defined within the DTD. For example:' => 'XML mengizinkan deklarasi entitas kustom di dalam DTD. Contohnya:',
    'This definition means that any usage of the entity reference [[C0]] within the XML document will be replaced with the defined value: "[[C1]]".' => 'Definisi ini membuat setiap kemunculan referensi [[C0]] dalam dokumen XML digantikan nilainya menjadi "[[C1]]".',
    'What are XML external entities?' => 'Apa itu XML external entity?',
    'XML external entities are a type of custom entity whose definition is located outside of the DTD where they are declared.' => 'XML external entity adalah entitas kustom yang definisinya diambil dari luar DTD tempat ia dideklarasikan.',
    'The declaration of an external entity uses the [[C0]] keyword and must specify a URL from which the value of the entity should be loaded. For example:' => 'Deklarasi external entity memakai kata kunci [[C0]] dan wajib menyertakan URL asal pemuatan nilainya. Contohnya:',
    'The URL can use the [[C0]] protocol, and so external entities can be loaded from file. For example:' => 'URL tersebut juga dapat memakai skema [[C0]] agar nilai entitas dimuat langsung dari file. Contohnya:',
    'XML external entities provide the primary means by which [[A0]]XML external entity attacks[[/A0]] arise.' => 'Fitur inilah yang menjadi celah utama terjadinya [[A0]]serangan XML external entity[[/A0]].',
];
